<title>USA: Allegiance unit to buy consulting firm.</title>
<headline>Allegiance unit to buy consulting firm.</headline>
<dateline>MCGAW PARK, Ill. 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Allegiance Corp said its U.S. unit will acquire  West Hudson &amp; Co Inc, a privately owned health-care consulting firm with annual sales of about $38 million.</p>
<p>Financial terms of the acquisition, expected to close January 2, were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Allegiance makes and markets medical, surgical and laboratory supplies. It was spun off earlier this year by Baxter International Inc.</p>
<p>West Hudson employs about 200 consultants across the United States who work full time at their client hospitals.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787))</p>
